From 2e1f99fe6b1df67edaa31486b9b55ec81f5ecc06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] dos: Count BEGIN_DIR cells over the stream creation
 rate

The stream creation limit (DoSStreamCreationEnabled, Rate and Burst)
applies a per-circuit token bucket to RELAY_BEGIN and RELAY_RESOLVE
cells, but connection_exit_begin_conn() hands BEGIN_DIR cells off before
it gets there. One way to defend against a BEGIN_DIR flood is to apply
the same limit to them; before choosing it over DoSBeginDirMaxStreams's
limit on open streams, we need to know what it would refuse.

Give each OR circuit a second bucket at the same rate and burst, for
BEGIN_DIR cells only, and count the cells that find it empty as
tor_relay_dos_total{type="begindir_over_stream_rate"}, whether or not
DoSStreamCreationEnabled is set. It never refuses anything, and leaves
the RELAY_BEGIN bucket alone. The check runs in
dos_should_refuse_begindir(), where stock tor would check a RELAY_BEGIN
cell: after the directory and hibernation checks. or_circuit_t grows by
one token_bucket_ctr_t. Only the MetricsPort shows this count, so a
relay without one leaves the bucket alone.

Part of #41339.
